  "publisher": "wyattdave",
  "notes": [
    "Workspace convention, not a CAP CLI input. Create one table at a time, in array order, with createDataverseTable(spec.tables[i], { cwd, environment: spec.environmentUrl, publish: true }).",
    "Reporter / comment author / history 'changed by' use Dataverse's server-stamped createdby, so no client-supplied reporter column exists.",
    "Issue status is a local choice with a fixed default workflow (see dist/config/app-config.js WORKFLOW). Board columns map to those status values.",
    "Alternate keys are not supported by the CAP table API. Add them manually after creation: wd_project(wd_key), wd_issue(wd_issuekey), wd_projectsequence(wd_project), wd_projectmember(wd_project + wd_user).",
    "Phase 2 order (existing tables are reused and only missing columns are added): wd_Sprint, wd_Issue (adds Story Points + Sprint), wd_BoardIssue, wd_IssueLink. Phase 2 alternate keys: wd_boardissue(wd_board + wd_issue), wd_issuelink(wd_fromissue + wd_toissue + wd_linktype).",
    "Phase 3 order: wd_Project (adds workflow columns), wd_Issue (adds Resolution), wd_WorkflowTransition, wd_SavedFilter, wd_Notification, wd_NotificationPreference, wd_IssueAttachment, wd_CustomField, wd_CustomFieldValue. CAP skips existing columns, so the four new Issue Status values (Backlog 100000004, Blocked 100000005, In Testing 100000006, Closed 100000007) are added to wd_issue.wd_status and wd_boardcolumn.wd_status with the InsertOptionValue Web API action. Phase 3 alternate keys: wd_workflowtransition(wd_project + wd_fromstatus + wd_tostatus), wd_notificationpreference(wd_user), wd_customfieldvalue(wd_issue + wd_customfield).",
    "Phase 4 order: wd_Version, wd_Issue (adds Original/Remaining Estimate, Time Spent, Fix Version, Started On), wd_WorkLog. Phase 4 alternate key: wd_version(wd_project + wd_name).",
    "Phase 5 order: wd_Issue (adds Solution Version), wd_EpicSolution. Phase 5 alternate key: wd_epicsolution(wd_issue + wd_stage)."
  ],
